  "term": "Alström–Hallgren syndrome",
  "definition": "Alström–Hallgren syndrome is a rare inherited disorder that affects multiple organs. It is marked by progressive vision loss, hearing loss, childhood obesity, and later endocrine, kidney, and liver problems, while mental development is typically normal.",
